//////javascript express
->>>app.use(express.json())
    this syntax tells the server how to handel the json data in express.


->>>app.use(express.urlencode({expanded:true}))
    this is used to read the data that were came form the html forms

  
->>>app.use(express.static('public'))
    by using this syntax we can access the html files under the public folder by express server

  
->>>app.get('/',async(req,res)=>{
      res.SendFile(path.join(__dirname,"public/index.html"))
      });
    this line is used to join the path of the current file and the file index.html file which is in the public folder.
    and also we are sending the html file to the client that's why we used sendfile and we were using
    current dirname because to understand from which basefolder we are using the code to send the client
    so that we were joining the html and the current folder.

->>>app.get('/:login',async (req,res)=>{
    res.SendFile(path.join(__dirname,"public/login.html"))});


